PR #5 promoted `HttpClient` from per-instance to `static final` shared singleton in both `OpenAIClient` and `OllamaClient`. The shared client's HTTP/1.1 connection pool reuses keep-alive connections — when llama.cpp closes idle connections server-side, subsequent requests on stale pooled connections throw `java.io.IOException: HTTP/1.1 header parser received no bytes`.

Reverted to per-instance `HttpClient` creation in both clients:

```java
// Before (PR #5): shared client reuses stale connections
private static final HttpClient HTTP_CLIENT = HttpClient.newHttpClient();

// After: fresh client per instance, no stale connection pool
private final HttpClient httpClient;
public OpenAIClient(...) {
    this.httpClient = HttpClient.newHttpClient();
}
```

- **`OpenAIClient.java`** — `static final HTTP_CLIENT` → instance field `httpClient`, restored constructor initialization
- **`OllamaClient.java`** — same revert

