Phase 1 UI implementation: Adds Updates section with placeholder data and "New update" button for authorized users. No database changes.

## Components Created (`src/components/updates/`)

- **UpdatesSection**: Container with title, list rendering, empty state, and conditional button
- **UpdateCard**: Individual update display (title, summary, date, optional author)
- **NewUpdateButton**: Client component with auth-gated UI (shows "Log in to post an update" when unauthenticated)

## Pages Modified

- **Projects** (`src/app/projects/[slug]/page.tsx`): Refactored existing Updates section to use reusable component, preserves existing `project_updates` query
- **Organisations** (`src/app/organisations/[id]/page.tsx`): Added Updates section with placeholder data
- **Watchdog** (`src/app/watchdog/[id]/page.tsx`): Created new issue detail page with Updates section

## Authorization

Uses existing patterns:
- `Boolean(user)` for authentication check
- `canEdit` (derived from creator/admin status) for post authorization
- Button stub shows alert: "Publishing updates coming soon!"

